 ## Operating characteristics
-**Time Complexity:** Construction is $O(N \log N)$, dominated by the first sorting pass. The second pass is $O((N/B) \cdot B \log B) = O(N \log B)$, which is subsumed if $B$ is constant [S1]. Initial extraction and average-case runtime complexity is $O(K)$, where $K$ is the number of active cells, making it output optimal [S1]. Worst-case performance is $O(N)$ [S1].
-**Memory Complexity:** The method incurs a $3 + 1/B$ factor increase in memory consumption relative to the input data, or $3 + 2/B$ if incremental search is desired. For large $B$, this factor is effectively 3 [S1].
