 **Strengths:** Simple implementation, output optimal average-case performance, works with floating-point and quantized data, small memory footprint [S1].
-**Limitations:** Worst-case $O(N)$ performance. The last active bucket requires checking all $B$ cells, which can be a bottleneck if $B$ is large and the isosurface is sparse in that region [S1].
-**When to use:** When output optimality is critical and the data distribution allows for efficient bucketing. Suitable for large-scale visualization systems where incremental extraction is beneficial [S1].
